From: j7
Subject: j7: double buffer the panel, and flip to the finished frame

The panel scans 0x67000000 continuously and present() wrote every row straight into it, so every
frame was torn and every store cost a bus transaction: 8.29 MB measured 34 ms, about 15 cycles a
word, which is store latency and not memory bandwidth.

Two contiguous scanout buffers in ordinary cacheable memory, painted alternately, cleaning the
finished one once and pointing the display controller's window 0 base at it. The controller reads
that base when it starts a frame, so the frame in flight keeps its own buffer and the next one
starts on the new one. Tearing goes, and the CPU writes at cache speed instead of one transaction
per word. The row shadow skip is off while flipping - the back buffer holds the frame from two
presents ago, not what is on the panel - and the power-off fade paints the buffer that is on
screen. j7fb_flip=0 keeps the loader's single buffer.

Co-Authored-By: dipa-studio <183933817+dipa-studio@users.noreply.github.com>

